#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151827 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b24db328-4a49-5002-b0af-635d0c0d89b9" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating the Step Function"}] :question/id #uuid "da59a348-2112-505c-824d-9e8df8409127" :question/math-academy-id "e-21591" :question/problem "Evaluate $f(t) = 9u(t-9)$ at $t=9$, where $u$ is the unit step function." :question/worked-solution "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{1, t \\ge 0,; 0, t < 0\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f(t)$ at $t=9$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(9) &= 9u(9 - 9) \\\\\n&= 9u(0) \\\\\n&= 9 \\cdot 1 \\\\\n&= 9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nf(9)=9\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151828 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f7a33f8-b0f6-5265-9d3e-c1ca34c07161" :knowledge-point/title "Graphs of Transformed Step Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "718a239f-9b43-5b4d-b638-b0f64be196fe" :question/math-academy-id "e-21592" :question/problem "The graph of $y=f(t)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be $f(t)$, where $u$ denotes the unit step function?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2760/Source/Images/b25aad85ae1374bd6c1bd86713ad24ca.png)" :question/worked-solution "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{1, t \\ge 0,; 0, t < 0\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y=u(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2760/Source/Images/cea5e5cfbce8e6708425a867337b8411.png)\n\nNotice that to transform $y=u(t)$ to the given function $y=f(t)$, we perform the following transformations:\n\n- First, we shift $y=u(t)$ by $2$ units to the left, giving $y=u(t+2)$.\n- Then, we scale $y=u(t+2)$ by a factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis, giving $y=3u(t+2)$.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(t)=3u(t+2)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151829 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "253b1011-a313-5004-8cbe-61133586e6b1" :knowledge-point/title "Graphs of Reflected Step Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "c13d67e8-db9e-5d02-a501-98f8987169fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-21594" :question/problem "The graph of $y = f(t)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be $f(t)$, where $u$ denotes the unit step function?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2760/Source/Images/6058d85fd3a0bb42589d8c84a6f4f946.png)" :question/worked-solution "The unit step function $u(t)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{1, t \\ge 0,; 0, t < 0\n$$\n\nThe graph of $y = u(t)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/2760/Source/Images/63ce6d8bac7002ace80730a3619b1370.png)\n\nNotice that to transform the function $y = u(t)$ to the given function $y = f(t)$, we perform the following transformations:\n\n- First, we reflect $y = u(t)$ in the $y$-axis, which gives $y = u(-t)$.\n- Next, we shift by one unit to the left, giving $y = u(-(t+1)) = u(-1 - t)$.\n- Finally, we scale by a scale factor of $2$ parallel to the $y$-axis, giving $y = 2u(-1 - t)$.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\nf(t) = 2u(-1 - t)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152479 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6f7a33f8-b0f6-5265-9d3e-c1ca34c07161" :knowledge-point/title "Graphs of Transformed Step Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1cb84a3-549d-594a-82ff-2a06cecb2df0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149715} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5146be-d10f-5232-8c82-42df43979d39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2u(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149716} {:answer/id #uuid "197e0a11-e23f-518f-9db4-c9f4a7cbd614" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(t - 1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149717} {:answer/id #uuid "2ffc47f5-1192-5d9c-ae20-15f8d828db63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149718} {:answer/id #uuid "666b50d8-b1c9-57d0-a1be-a32919cd4de2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2u(t)